{"call_id":"5f08e414-ee3d-477e-8dc2-1a8c3911a15b","metadata":{"error_type":null,"finish_reason":"stop","mode":"ok","response_id":"1a62b3f09c71cee0b0a1f1902e7d580b.90910b57ab3e4b3d6191dd067bf79d0f","status_code":null,"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cached_tokens":4096,"completion_tokens":4488,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":0,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"prompt_tokens":5479,"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cache_write_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":4096,"image_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"total_tokens":9967}},"raw_response":{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null,"message":{"annotations":null,"audio":null,"content":"```json\n{\n  \"protocol_version\": \"impact-response-v3\",\n  \"action\": \"read\",\n  \"summary\": \"New section 订单导出 exists in S2 but is not covered by supplied fixed_text_evidence; request its original text to assess the added rule.\",\n  \"reads\": {\n    \"ranges\": [\n      {\n        \"source_ref\": \"S2\",\n        \"start_char\": 93,\n        \"end_char\": 139\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```","function_call":null,"reasoning":"The user wants me to analyze document impact based on the fixed evidence provided. Let me carefully review the protocol and the data.\n\nKey instructions:\n1. Return one impact-response-v3 JSON object using response_schema.\n2. Use short S/P/C/D references for reads.\n3. In discovery, document_citations is a list of T references from fixed_text_evidence; select supplied original text, never calculate/copy offsets, quotes, UUIDs or hashes.\n4. The server binds each T to its exact original text/position/hash and verifies it.\n5. T entries are actual text evidence, other catalogs are retrieval metadata.\n6. For action=read supply reads with no final candidates/outcome; for finish provide unit_outcome/candidates/unresolved with no pending reads.\n7. During case_impacts return BoundRuleCaseAssessment: rule_ref R1 etc. plus case_impacts for every supplied fixed rule.\n8. The server retains each original rule and its citations.\n9. Case citations use literal JSON paths and actual values from a supplied complete case.\n10. Keep intentional negative conditions.\n11. Request fixed reads for missing/cross-section evidence.\n12. All candidates need review, deployment remains unknown; do not claim full coverage or execute/change official records.\n13. This schema defines the wire reply, canonical identities mentioned in coordination instructions belong to the server.\n\nCurrent stage: discover_rules. There are no rules supplied yet (rules: []). So I need to propose rule candidates based on the document changes.\n\nThe fixed source catalog shows:\n- S1 (old): parse:75cd7d9b-84a4-43a8-98af-e4bee2c2a9ed, length 126, sections:\n  - section-1: 订单服务需求 (0-126)\n    - section-2: 订单保留 (12-48)\n    - section-3: 优惠码 (48-83)\n    - section-4: 管理鉴权 (83-126)\n- S2 (new): parse:51a9af8f-492e-43cf-a793-688fdb61bc32, length 139, sections:\n  - section-1: 订单服务需求 (0-139)\n    - section-2: 订单保留 (12-48)\n    - section-3: 管理鉴权 (48-93)  <- wait, 管理鉴权 moved up?\n    - section-4: 订单导出 (93-139)\n\nWait, in S2 sections:\n- section-3: 管理鉴权 (48-93) - this seems to replace 优惠码?\n- section-4: 订单导出 (93-139) - new section\n\nActually, looking at the text evidence:\nT1 (old S1, chars 21-81): \"已支付订单保留7天，超过保留期查询返回410。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 优惠码\\r\\n提交有效优惠码PROMO5时订单金额减少5元。\\r\\n\"\nT2 (new S2, chars 21-46): \"已支付订单保留9天，超过保留期查询返回410。\\r\\n\"\n\nSo the changes are:\n1. \"7天\" -> \"9天\" (修改 retention period)\n2. The \"优惠码\" section was deleted (from old) and \"订单导出\" section added (in new).\n3. In new S2, 管理鉴权 section spans chars 48-93, while old 管理鉴权 was 83-126. The 优惠码 section (48-83 in old) is gone.\n\nThe primary difference D1 shows:\n- Replace \"7\" with \"9\"\n- Delete \"。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 优惠码\\r\\n提交有效优惠码PROMO5时订单金额减少5元\"\n- Overall replace old text (retention + promo code) with new text (only retention)\n\nSo rule candidates:\n- Rule 1: Modified - 订单保留天数从7天改为9天 (Order retention period changed from 7 to 9 days)\n- Rule 2: Removed - 优惠码规则被删除 (Promo code rule removed)\n- Rule 3: Added - 新增订单导出规则 (New order export rule) - but I don't have the actual text for 订单导出. I only know the section exists in new (93-139) but no text evidence T reference shown for it. The fixed_text_evidence only has T1 and T2. I don't have actual quote for 订单导出 section. According to instructions, document_citations must be T references from fixed_text_evidence. I only have T1 and T2. T1 covers old retention + promo code. T2 covers new retention. I don't have T for new 订单导出 section. So I cannot cite it. I should note this as uncertain or request a read. But wait, I can request reads in action=read. Should I request a read for the 订单导出 section? The instruction says: \"Request fixed reads for missing/cross-section evidence.\" So yes, I should issue action=read to request the missing evidence for the new 订单导出 section. But wait, in discovery, do I need to read more before finishing? The user input has stage discover_rules and rules []. The protocol says: \"For action=read supply reads with no final candidates/outcome; for finish provide unit_outcome/candidates/unresolved with no pending reads.\"\n\nI have enough evidence for retention change and promo removal, but not for the new export section. I can either finish with those two rules and note unresolved for export, or request a read. The instruction \"Request fixed reads for missing/cross-section evidence\" suggests I should request reads. But the user is asking me to respond. Typically in these agentic loops, I can choose action=read to request more data. However, the final output should be one impact-response-v3 JSON. Let me check if I should finish or read.\n\nActually, looking at the S2 sections, 订单导出 is section-4 at chars 93-139. But I don't have the text. The fixed_text_evidence has only T1 and T2. To properly assess the added 订单导出 rule, I need to read