idence is supplied; request original text to assess added rule.\",\n  \"reads\": {\n    \"ranges\": [\n      {\n        \"source_ref\": \"S2\",\n        \"start_char\": 93,\n        \"end_char\": 139\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIs there any need to include `candidates` empty? Schema allows but not required. Better to omit to keep clean. `unit_outcome` should be omitted or null? The protocol says \"for finish provide unit_outcome...\". For read, we should not provide it. Schema default null but not required? Actually unit_outcome is not in required. Omitting is fine. But some validators might expect it absent for read. I'll omit.\n\nWait, the schema properties include unit_outcome but required only protocol_version, action, summary. So omit.\n\nDouble-check \"additionalProperties\": false at root. So I cannot add extra fields. Good.\n\nI think that's the correct response.","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to analyze document impact based on the fixed evidence provided. Let me carefully review the protocol and the data.\n\nKey instructions:\n1. Return one impact-response-v3 JSON object using response_schema.\n2. Use short S/P/C/D references for reads.\n3. In discovery, document_citations is a list of T references from fixed_text_evidence; select supplied original text, never calculate/copy offsets, quotes, UUIDs or hashes.\n4. The server binds each T to its exact original text/position/hash and verifies it.\n5. T entries are actual text evidence, other catalogs are retrieval metadata.\n6. For action=read supply reads with no final candidates/outcome; for finish provide unit_outcome/candidates/unresolved with no pending reads.\n7. During case_impacts return BoundRuleCaseAssessment: rule_ref R1 etc. plus case_impacts for every supplied fixed rule.\n8. The server retains each original rule and its citations.\n9. Case citations use literal JSON paths and actual values from a supplied complete case.\n10. Keep intentional negative conditions.\n11. Request fixed reads for missing/cross-section evidence.\n12. All candidates need review, deployment remains unknown; do not claim full coverage or execute/change official records.\n13. This schema defines the wire reply, canonical identities mentioned in coordination instructions belong to the server.\n\nCurrent stage: discover_rules. There are no rules supplied yet (rules: []). So I need to propose rule candidates based on the document changes.\n\nThe fixed source catalog shows:\n- S1 (old): parse:75cd7d9b-84a4-43a8-98af-e4bee2c2a9ed, length 126, sections:\n  - section-1: 订单服务需求 (0-126)\n    - section-2: 订单保留 (12-48)\n    - section-3: 优惠码 (48-83)\n    - section-4: 管理鉴权 (83-126)\n- S2 (new): parse:51a9af8f-492e-43cf-a793-688fdb61bc32, length 139, sections:\n  - section-1: 订单服务需求 (0-139)\n    - section-2: 订单保留 (12-48)\n    - section-3: 管理鉴权 (48-93)  <- wait, 管理鉴权 moved up?\n    - section-4: 订单导出 (93-139)\n\nWait, in S2 sections:\n- section-3: 管理鉴权 (48-93) - this seems to replace 优惠码?\n- section-4: 订单导出 (93-139) - new section\n\nActually, looking at the text evidence:\nT1 (old S1, chars 21-81): \"已支付订单保留7天，超过保留期查询返回410。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 优惠码\\r\\n提交有效优惠码PROMO5时订单金额减少5元。\\r\\n\"\nT2 (new S2, chars 21-46): \"已支付订单保留9天，超过保留期查询返回410。\\r\\n\"\n\nSo the changes are:\n1. \"7天\" -> \"9天\" (修改 retention period)\n2. The \"优惠码\" section was deleted (from old) and \"订单导出\" section added (in new).\n3. In new S2, 管理鉴权 section spans chars 48-93, while old 管理鉴权 was 83-126. The 优惠码 section (48-83 in old) is gone.\n\nThe primary difference D1 shows:\n- Replace \"7\" with \"9\"\n- Delete \"。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 优惠码\\r\\n提交有效优惠码PROMO5时订单金额减少5元\"\n- Overall replace old text (retention + promo code) with new text (only retention)\n\nSo rule candidates:\n- Rule 1: Modified - 订单保留天数从7天改为9天 (Order retention period changed from 7 to 9 days)\n- Rule 2: Removed - 优惠码规则被删除 (Promo code rule removed)\n- Rule 3: Added - 新增订单导出规则 (New order export rule) - but I don't have the actual text for 订单导出. I only know the section exis